  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting the mainstreaming of biodiversity and protection of ecosystem services through regenerative and deforestation-free livestock in provinces of Manab&#xc3;&#xad;, Pichincha and Morona-Santiago.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establish regenerative and deforestation-free management in livestock production in the provinces of Manab&#xc3;&#xad;, Morona Santiago and Pichincha, as a comprehensive approach to conserve biodiversity, protect ecosystem services and generate measurable global environmental benefits.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is designed to generate significant socio-economic benefits at both national and local levels by promoting sustainable management and improving market access for goods produced in this way. In particular, the project contributes to the following benefits:?      Reducing vulnerabilities: By improving local adaptation to climate change, the project will help reduce the vulnerability of communities, ensuring they can better cope with future environmental challenges, resulting in increased resilience of livestock landscapes. ?      Improving food security: By promoting sustainable livestock management, the project will contribute to more efficient and resilient production, which in turn will improve food security in local territories.?      Developing capacities: Through ongoing training workshops, the project will build local capacities and skills of producers and other stakeholders, enhancing their ability to adapt to environmental and economic changes.?      Promoting entrepreneurship: Supporting the development of small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) in sustainable sectors will generate new business opportunities, thereby diversifying the local economy.?      Improving food security and nutrition: By increasing and diversifying the availability of nutritious foods through RDF management, the project will contribute to improving nutrition, which has a positive impact on the health and well-being of the population.These socioeconomic benefits directly support the achievement of global environmental benefits by promoting biodiversity conservation, encouraging climate-adapted RDF livestock management, and improving ecosystem services on each of the producers&apos; farms. Similarly, they contribute to adaptation benefits by increasing the resilience of territories to climate impacts, ensuring that they have the tools and knowledge necessary to adapt to changing environmental conditions.Furthermore, the project will also contribute to improving rural employment and economic opportunities by strengthening social protection and empowering rural communities. The project will promote the creation of employment opportunities in rural communities through the implementation of RDF management, which will allow producers to diversify their sources of income and improve their economic security.</narrative>
  </description>
